WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.897
This slide summarizes the main organization tools from the module.

00:00:03.897 --> 00:00:08.507
Use a function when you need one reusable task.

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:14.782
For example, get_profit can calculate profit from sales and costs.

00:00:14.782 --> 00:00:19.217
Use a module when you have a file of related functions or constants.

00:00:19.217 --> 00:00:23.887
For example, metrics.py might store several metric calculations.

00:00:23.887 --> 00:00:31.577
Use a package when a project has several related modules that should be grouped together.

00:00:31.577 --> 00:00:38.762
For example, analytics_tools could be a folder containing cleaning, metrics, and reporting modules.

00:00:38.762 --> 00:00:43.132
Use a class when data and behavior belong together.

00:00:43.132 --> 00:00:49.452
For example, SalesReport stores sales data and provides methods for total sales, average sales,

00:00:49.452 --> 00:00:55.962
and high sales count. Use an object when you need one real instance created from a class.

00:00:55.962 --> 00:01:01.007
For example, report equals SalesReport creates one working report object.

00:01:01.007 --> 00:01:04.142
The practical rule is to start with functions.

00:01:04.142 --> 00:01:10.112
Move to modules when the file becomes long.

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:14.407
Use classes when one concept has both data and actions.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:18.625
This decision-making skill is more important than memorizing syntax.
